# BLOG

# Rhythm Culture Blog – Drumming, Dancing & Community

Welcome to the **Rhythm Culture blog**, a place to explore the world of African drumming, African dance, music, movement and community connection. Here we'll share stories, ideas, inspiration and insights from our workshops, classes, school incursions and events, celebrating the power of rhythm to bring people together.

At Rhythm Culture, we believe that music and movement are for everyone. You don't need previous musical experience or dance skills to join in, just a willingness to have a go, get involved and enjoy the experience. Through African drumming and dancing, we create opportunities for people of all ages and abilities to connect, express themselves, learn something new and share in the energy of making music together.

Our blog will take you behind the scenes of Rhythm Culture, sharing highlights from our African drumming workshops, school incursions, African dance classes, community gatherings and corporate team-building experiences. You'll discover more about the instruments we play, the rhythms we explore, the traditions that inspire our work and the many ways drumming and dancing can bring groups together.

We'll also share ideas for incorporating rhythm and movement into schools, workplaces and community settings, along with updates about upcoming workshops, classes, visiting artists and special events.

Whether you're a teacher looking for an engaging African drumming incursion for your students, an organisation interested in a unique team-building workshop, or someone who simply loves music, dance and connecting with others, we hope you'll find something here to inspire you.

Rhythm is universal. It crosses boundaries, creates connection and reminds us of the joy of doing something together.

So take a look around, explore our stories and, most importantly, don't be afraid to find your rhythm!

**Welcome to Rhythm Culture – where drumming, dancing and community come together.**
